Void Linux rice (experimental)
==============================

The experimental machine. Arch is the daily driver; this is where new ideas
get tried first. Saved 2026-10-21 from the live Void install. Nothing here is
managed by Home Manager or Nix.

Stack: Void Linux, runit + xbps (no systemd), MangoWC, DankMaterialShell
(DMS), kitty, Maple Mono NF.

Layout
------

wm/            the `wm` repo copy: Mango config (wm/config/mango/config.conf),
               fontconfig, rofi, install script
home/          ~/.bashrc, ~/.aliases (xbps/runit versions of the Arch aliases)
config/        ~/.config copies: dms, fastfetch, kitty, nvim, fuzzel, swayosd,
               flameshot, spotify, variety, codium-insiders
bin/           ~/.local/bin wrappers for the Flatpaks (zen-browser, spotify,
               code-insiders)
etc-xbps.d/    DMS repository files for /etc/xbps.d
packages/      xbps-manual.txt (manually installed), flatpak.txt

~/.face (profile picture) is deliberately not committed -- the repo is public.

Differences from the Arch setup
-------------------------------

- Shell: DMS (`dms run`) instead of caelestia-shell-mango. The old caelestia
  keybinds are mapped to `dms ipc call ...`.
- Packages: xbps instead of pacman/paru; Zen, Spotify and VSCodium Insiders
  come from Flatpak.
- Services: runit (sv, /var/service) instead of systemd. The service aliases
  are converted.
- Disabled on Void: mangobar, mako, variety, wallpaper-manager autostart and
  the wm theme engine. DMS owns bar, notifications, wallpaper and colours.
- wm/config/themes/theme-engine.py no longer calls update_fastfetch(); it used
  to overwrite the fastfetch config on every theme apply.
- Every new terminal runs fastfetch (end of home/.bashrc).

Restore on a fresh Void install
-------------------------------

1. Copy etc-xbps.d/* to /etc/xbps.d/, then `sudo xbps-install -Su` and
   `sudo xbps-install -S dms matugen cava qt6-multimedia`. Check the repo
   signing-key fingerprint against the official docs before accepting it.
2. Install what is in packages/xbps-manual.txt that you want.
3. `flatpak install --user flathub` the IDs in packages/flatpak.txt.
4. Copy home/ into ~, config/* into ~/.config, and bin/* into ~/.local/bin.
5. Link or copy wm/config/* per wm/install.sh; the Mango config is
   wm/config/mango/config.conf.
6. Wallpapers are not in this repo (about 4.8G). Put them in
   ~/Pictures/wallpapers.

Known loose ends
----------------

- VSCodium extensions are not installed; the list is in
  config/codium-insiders/extensions.txt.
- The flameshot save path still points at a folder from the Arch machine.
- The Zen browser profile is not migrated.
